    {
      "id": "claim_849b84be7a024670aa6618a9b0e372f0",
      "statement": "Keychain writes follow the planKeychainWrites ordering — delete removed instance keys, write the fingerprint index, write instance keys, sync the active pointer last — so any interruption window lands on an existing self-healing path and never leaves orphan instance keys outside the index; the legacy single-credential key is migrated idempotently on read, and tokens live only in Keychain (never MMKV or logs).",
