    {
      "id": "claim_b022102449bf44ddb6e6e4df83acfb7c",
      "statement": "Verified serviceKey→fingerprint associations are held by the provider and shared across sessions for the app session in memory, so one session's verification lets others reuse or exclude candidates and prevents a probe storm under parallel sessions; an auth terminal state (unauthorized/revoked) observed by a session removes only that instance's credentials.",
